From ef74d464aeee4e60c08dc003a94c5959a7bf80eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:24:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] misc: add Goodix ultrasonic fingerprint control for NX809J

Add power, reset and interrupt control for the GUM5228 ultrasonic stack
identified in NX809J's stock fingerprint init configuration. Keep the SPI
bus under QTEE ownership; biometric commands use the signed goodixfp64
trusted application through /dev/tee0.

Wire reset GPIO 215, IRQ GPIO 99 and the PM8010-M L7 supply from the stock
device tree. Match the stock module's rising-edge interrupt and 10 ms
reset-low / 5 ms recovery sequence. Expose a root-only, exclusive-open
control node with interrupt polling, power-off on close and suspend
blocking while the sensor is powered.

Enable the driver in NX809J's configuration and document the binding and
native UAPI. No Android netlink, input injection or panel callbacks are
needed for this initial platform-control interface.

Validation: strict checkpatch passes; the configuration audit adds only
GOODIX_TEE_FP=y; the NX809J DTB compiles through devices-build. The full
kernel build is blocked by unrelated missing mpss_mem, q6_mpss_dtb_mem,
dsm_partition_1_mem and dsm_partition_2_mem references when building
kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dtb. Hardware validation awaits a reboot; the
phone has not been flashed or rebooted.

Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 5c9fbb6c26c953b50e11d3d6d4d7df41f07940bf)
